and_doc_webhook_intro_title === Introduction
and_doc_webhook_intro_line1 === Webhooks are a powerful feature that let your server listen for events from your devices or WhatsApp. This helps you automate tasks.
and_doc_webhook_intro_line2 === This feature only works for incoming events like SMS, WhatsApp messages, USSD responses, and Android notifications.
and_doc_webhook_usecases_title === Use Cases
and_doc_webhook_usecase1 === Auto-reply bot for SMS and WhatsApp.
and_doc_webhook_usecase2 === Save messages and chats to your database.
and_doc_webhook_usecase3 === Save notifications to your database.
and_doc_webhook_usecase4 === Save USSD replies to your database.
and_doc_webhook_usecase5 === Send payloads to email addresses.
and_doc_webhook_usecase6 === Send an SMS or chat when you get a Facebook notification.
and_doc_webhook_usecase7 === Run actions when a notification is received from any app.
and_doc_webhook_how_title === How It Works
and_doc_webhook_how_line1 === When an event is received, the system sends it to your webhook URL using the POST method. Your server can then handle the payload however you want.
and_doc_webhook_flow_image_alt === Webhook Flow
and_doc_webhook_payload_title === Payload Structure
and_doc_webhook_payload_line1 === Each payload has a type and data. You just need to check the type and process the data.
and_doc_webhook_payload_sms === SMS
and_doc_webhook_payload_whatsapp === WhatsApp
and_doc_webhook_payload_ussd === USSD
and_doc_webhook_payload_notification === Notification
and_doc_webhook_code_title === Code Example
and_doc_actions_intro_title === Introduction
and_doc_actions_intro_line1 === Actions are tools that help automate tasks like listening for send/receive events or automatically replying to messages.
and_doc_actions_intro_line2 === They are designed specifically for SMS and WhatsApp related automation.
and_doc_actions_types_title === Types of Actions
and_doc_actions_type_hooks === Hooks
and_doc_actions_type_hooks_desc === Hooks listen for SMS/WhatsApp send and receive events. Unlike webhooks, they also support send events and use the GET method. You can structure the URL yourself.
and_doc_actions_type_autoreplies === Autoreplies
and_doc_actions_type_autoreplies_desc === Autoreplies automatically respond to incoming messages when a keyword is detected. You set the keywords and the response message.
and_doc_actions_usecases_title === Use Cases
and_doc_actions_usecase1 === Log events to your server when you send or receive a message.
and_doc_actions_usecase2 === Call a remote URL on message send/receive.
and_doc_actions_usecase3 === Automatically reply if a keyword is found in a message.
and_doc_actions_how_title === How It Works
and_doc_actions_how_line1 === The images below explain how hooks and autoreplies work.
