and_doc_android_intro_title === Introduction
and_doc_android_intro_line1 === To send and receive SMS messages, you need to link Android devices with SIM card support. Sending SMS requires carrier balance.
and_doc_android_versions_title === Android Support
and_doc_android_versions_line1 === The gateway app supports the following Android versions:
and_doc_android_version_oreo === Android Oreo
and_doc_android_version_pie === Android Pie
and_doc_android_version_10 === Android 10
and_doc_android_version_11 === Android 11
and_doc_android_version_12 === Android 12
and_doc_android_version_13 === Android 13
and_doc_android_version_14 === Android 14
and_doc_android_version_15 === Android 15
and_doc_android_receive_title === Receiving SMS
and_doc_android_receive_line1 === You can disable SMS receiving from a device if it is only used for sending.
and_doc_android_receive_line2 === Note: this will also disable receive-related features such as webhooks.
and_doc_android_interval_title === Send Interval
and_doc_android_interval_line1 === Use this to avoid SMS spam issues. Messages will send at random intervals based on the min and max seconds you define.
and_doc_android_notifications_title === Notifications
and_doc_android_notifications_line1 === The platform can listen to Android notifications and help automate tasks.
and_doc_android_notifications_line2 === Set app package names in the APPLICATIONS field of the device. Use line breaks to separate each package.
and_doc_android_partner_title === Partner Settings
and_doc_android_partner_line1 === Partners can access special device settings including global device access and rate controls.
and_doc_partner_intro_title === Introduction
and_doc_partner_intro_line1 === Our partnership system lets you earn by sharing your devices with other users to send messages on your local network.
and_doc_partner_intro_line2 === You control your partner devices completely. You can enable both SIM cards and set random send intervals.
and_doc_partner_earning_title === Earnings Potential
and_doc_partner_earning_case1 === A user from country X wants to send messages to your country Y. If your device is partnered, they can send local messages using your device at a lower cost.
and_doc_partner_earning_case2 === A user in your own country can also use your partnered device if they don’t have one.
and_doc_partner_how_title === How does it work?
and_doc_partner_how_alt === Diagram showing how the partner system works
and_doc_partner_apply_title === How to apply?
and_doc_partner_apply_line1 === If you're interested in becoming a partner, please contact us so we can upgrade your account.
